.TH KMD 1 "2026-11-24" "kmd 0.17.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kmd \- beautiful Markdown previews in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kmd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR ...]
.br
.B cat
\fIFILE\fR |
.B kmd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kmd
renders Markdown documents as rich, colorful previews in the terminal.
It implements CommonMark 0.31.2 and GitHub Flavored Markdown (tables, task
lists, strikethrough, extended autolinks), footnotes, GitHub alerts, emoji
shortcodes such as \fB:rocket:\fR and wiki links (\fB[[Page]]\fR,
\fB[[Page#Heading|label]]\fR, links to \fIPage\fB.md\fR next to the document),
and adds syntax highlighting, clickable OSC 8 hyperlinks, inline images,
Mermaid diagrams (flowchart, state, sequence, class, entity\-relationship,
Gantt and pie), Graphviz diagrams and LaTeX math rendered with Unicode.
.PP
With no \fIFILE\fR, or when \fIFILE\fR is \fB\-\fR, standard input is read.
A \fIFOLDER\fR shows its \fBREADME.md\fR (or \fBindex.md\fR); a folder without
one opens the viewer's file picker (see \fBFILE PICKER\fR), which lists every
Markdown file under it. When standard output is not a terminal, the folder is
printed as a list of its Markdown files and subfolders (hidden entries
excluded, at most 2000 entries read). Links to folders in documents behave
the same way.
Long documents are shown in the built\-in viewer when standard output is a
terminal (see \fBVIEWER\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Render width in columns. Defaults to the terminal width, capped at 110.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Color theme: a bundled theme, a user theme, or a path to a \fB.theme\fR file.
The default \fBauto\fR picks a dark or light theme (see \fBTHEMES\fR).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color " " \fIWHEN\fR
Use colors: \fBauto\fR (default), \fBalways\fR or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-images " " \fIMODE\fR
How to draw images: \fBauto\fR, \fBblocks\fR (Unicode half blocks),
\fBkitty\fR, \fBiterm2\fR, \fBsixel\fR or \fBnone\fR. Only local files and
data: URIs are displayed; remote images are never downloaded.
.TP
.BR \-\-hyperlinks " " \fIWHEN\fR
Emit clickable OSC 8 links: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-math
Show LaTeX source instead of rendered formulas.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-diagrams
Show Mermaid and Graphviz source instead of diagrams.
.TP
.B \-\-commonmark
Strict CommonMark: disable all GitHub extensions, emoji shortcodes and wiki
links.
.TP
.B \-\-base " " \fIURL\fR
Resolve the relative links of a document read from standard input against
\fIURL\fR, the address the document came from, as a browser would: with
\fBcurl \-fsSL https://example.com/docs/README.md | kmd \-\-base
https://example.com/docs/README.md\fR, \fB[guide](guide.md)\fR links to
\fBhttps://example.com/docs/guide.md\fR. Only \fBhttp\fR and \fBhttps\fR
URLs without a user name are accepted. Applies to the terminal output, the
viewer and \fB\-\-html\fR. Only inline \fBdata:\fR images are then drawn;
nothing is ever downloaded (see \fBREMOTE DOCUMENTS\fR).
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-no\-pager
Never page long output (no viewer).
.TP
.B \-\-view
Open the viewer even when the document fits on the screen.
.SS Output modes
.TP
.B \-\-toc
Print only the table of contents.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-section " " \fINAME\fR
Show only one section: the heading whose anchor is \fINAME\fR (with or
without \fB#\fR, as in \fB#getting\-started\fR), or else the first heading
whose text contains \fINAME\fR, ignoring case, and everything under it up to
the next heading of the same or a higher level. Works with \fB\-\-toc\fR,
\fB\-\-html\fR and the viewer. Exits with status 1 when no heading matches.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Export a standalone HTML page using the selected theme colors. Documents are
treated as untrusted: raw HTML is omitted, \fBjavascript:\fR, \fBvbscript:\fR,
\fBfile:\fR and non-image \fBdata:\fR URLs are dropped, and the page carries a
restrictive Content-Security-Policy. Code blocks are highlighted (the first
1 MiB of code of a document) and mermaid and Graphviz diagrams drawn as in
the terminal, with inline styles and no scripts (\fB\-\-no\-diagrams\fR
keeps their source). With \fB\-\-slides\fR, export the deck
instead: one 16:9 slide per section with its footer, one per page when
printed, so the browser's \fBPrint to PDF\fR makes a PDF deck (pauses
show the whole slide; notes are left out, even with \fB\-\-unsafe\-html\fR;
content taller than a slide is cut). The colors are the theme's: pick a
light one with \fB\-t\fR for paper.
.TP
.B \-\-unsafe\-html
With \fB\-\-html\fR: keep raw HTML and every URL. Use only with trusted input.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Live preview: re-render the file whenever it changes. On a terminal this
happens in the viewer, which keeps the scroll position and lets links be
followed (the document on screen is the one watched); quit with \fBq\fR.
With \fB\-P\fR, or when the output is not a terminal, the screen is redrawn
instead; stop with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B \-\-slides
Present the document as slides in the viewer: it is split at every
top\-level thematic break (\fB\-\-\-\fR), or, when there is none, before
every level 1 and 2 heading, and each slide is shown centered (rendered at
most 80 columns wide unless \fB\-\-width\fR is given). \fBRight\fR,
\fBSpace\fR, \fBPgDn\fR, \fBn\fR and \fBEnter\fR go to the next step or slide;
\fBLeft\fR, \fBPgUp\fR, \fBp\fR and \fBBackspace\fR to the previous one;
\fBg\fR and \fBG\fR to the first and last; \fBj\fR and \fBk\fR scroll a slide
taller than the screen. A \fB<!\-\- pause \-\->\fR line between blocks
reveals a slide in steps: going forward shows the next part and going back
hides it, and a list without blank lines between its items carries on
after a pause without a gap when it keeps the same marker.
Images on a slide are drawn with the terminal's graphics protocol
(\fB\-\-images\fR; sixel only when the terminal reports its cell size), at
most as tall as the screen and within the usual image limits; one that
does not fit whole on the screen is not drawn until it does.
The bottom line is a footer with the slide number and the \fBtitle\fR and
\fBauthor\fR from the front matter; a \fBfooter:\fR key there sets its
text (empty: only the number), and \fBfooter: false\fR (or \fBoff\fR) hides it.
Speaker notes go in \fB<!\-\- notes: ... \-\->\fR comments, never shown on
the slide; see \fB\-\-notes\fR.
Web links and files open as in the viewer; linked
Markdown documents do not. Works with \fB\-f\fR (the slides are re\-rendered
when the file changes) and \fB\-s\fR. Needs a terminal, except with
\fB\-\-html\fR, which writes the deck as a page instead (see \fB\-\-html\fR;
not with \fB\-f\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-notes
In a second terminal, show the speaker notes of the slide that
\fBkmd \-\-slides\fR, run on the same file, has on screen (notes are per
slide, not per step), and the title of the next slide. They follow the
presentation as it moves and are rendered again when the file changes;
when the presentation ends they stay on its last slide. The two share the
slide number through a state file in \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kmd\fR, or
\fIkmd\-<uid>\fR in the temporary directory, which must belong to the user
with mode 0700. Works with \fB\-s\fR (give the same section as the
presentation). Needs a terminal.
.SS Themes and configuration
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
List bundled and user themes with a color preview.
.TP
.B \-\-theme\-template " " \fINAME\fR
Print a bundled theme as an editable \fB.theme\fR file.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Show the configuration file location, the effective settings and a template.
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-\-completion " " \fISHELL\fR
Print a completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR or \fBfish\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kmd/config\fR (by default
\fI~/.config/kmd/config\fR), one \fBkey = value\fR per line; \fB#\fR starts a
comment. Keys: \fBtheme\fR, \fBdark-theme\fR, \fBlight-theme\fR, \fBwidth\fR,
\fBmax-width\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBimages\fR, \fBimage-rows\fR,
\fBhyperlinks\fR, \fBpager\fR, \fBmouse\fR, \fBview\fR, \fBmath\fR, \fBdiagrams\fR.
Relative values of \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR and \fBHOME\fR are ignored.
Command-line options take precedence over environment variables, which take
precedence over the configuration file.
.SH VIEWER
The built\-in viewer pages through long documents and follows their links.
Links to Markdown files open in the viewer itself, at the right heading when
the link has a \fB#anchor\fR, and \fBBackspace\fR goes back; web links,
\fBmailto:\fR links and local images or PDFs are handed to the desktop
(\fBxdg\-open\fR, or \fBopen\fR on macOS). Images are drawn with Unicode
blocks in the viewer, since terminal graphics cannot scroll with the text
(except in slides, see \fB\-\-slides\fR).
.TP
.B Tab\fR, \fBShift\-Tab
Select the next or previous link (or click a link with the mouse; a link
that leaves kmd is selected by the first click and opened by the second).
.TP
.B Enter\fR, \fBl\fR, \fBRight
Open the selected link.
.TP
.B Backspace\fR, \fBh\fR, \fBLeft
Go back to the previous document (or position, after an in\-page link).
.TP
.B H
Go back to the first document, the one kmd was started with.
.TP
.B j\fR, \fBk\fR, \fBSpace\fR, \fBb\fR, \fBd\fR, \fBu\fR, \fBg\fR, \fBG
Scroll by a line, a page, half a page; go to the top or the bottom (arrow,
page and Home/End keys and the mouse wheel work too).
.TP
.B t
Show the table of contents over the page, opened at the section being read:
move with \fBj\fR/\fBk\fR or the arrows, \fBEnter\fR (or a click) jumps to
the heading, \fBEsc\fR closes it. \fBBackspace\fR returns to where the jump
started.
.TP
.B [\fR, \fB]
Go to the previous or next section (heading).
.TP
.B o
Open the file picker for the folder kmd was started on: the document's
folder, the current folder for several files or standard input, or the
folder on screen; see \fBFILE PICKER\fR.
.TP
.B S
Open the file picker in text search mode.
.TP
.B c
Copy the source of a code block on screen to the clipboard; pressing
\fBc\fR again copies the next block on screen. Control characters other than
tab and newline are removed. Locally the text is given to \fBwl\-copy\fR,
\fBxclip\fR or \fBxsel\fR (\fBpbcopy\fR on macOS); over SSH, or when none is
installed, the terminal is asked to set the clipboard (OSC 52).
.TP
.B /\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBN
Search (case\-insensitive unless the text has capitals); next and previous match.
.TP
.B e
Edit the file with \fB$VISUAL\fR or \fB$EDITOR\fR, then reload it.
.TP
.B r\fR, \fB?\fR, \fBq
Reload, help, quit.
.PP
With \fBmouse = off\fR in the configuration file the terminal keeps the
mouse (clicks do not reach the viewer). Set \fBpager\fR or \fBKMD_PAGER\fR to
a command such as \fBless \-R\fR to use an external pager instead.
.SS FILE PICKER
The picker lists every Markdown file under a folder by its relative path,
filtered as you type (fuzzy and case\-insensitive: the typed letters must
appear in order, best matches first). \fBUp\fR/\fBDown\fR (\fBCtrl\-P\fR/\fBCtrl\-N\fR), \fBPgUp\fR/\fBPgDn\fR,
\fBHome\fR/\fBEnd\fR and the wheel choose; \fBEnter\fR or a click opens the
document, and \fBBackspace\fR in it returns to the list as it was.
\fBBackspace\fR deletes a character (on an empty filter over a document, it
closes the picker) and \fBCtrl\-U\fR clears the filter; \fBEsc\fR clears it,
or closes the picker, as do \fBCtrl\-C\fR and \fBCtrl\-G\fR.
.PP
\fBTab\fR switches to text search: type the text and press \fBEnter\fR to
search every listed document (case\-insensitive unless the text has capitals).
Matches are listed with their file, line and section; \fBEnter\fR opens the
document at that section with the text highlighted. The search runs in the
background and \fBEsc\fR cancels it.
.PP
The listing skips hidden files and folders (such as \fB.git\fR), \fBnode_modules\fR and
\fBvendor\fR, stays on the folder's file system, never enters symlinked
folders, and lists a symlinked document only when it points directly at a
regular Markdown file inside the folder (at most 1,000 are checked). It stops
at 20 levels, 10,000 documents or 200,000 directory entries, and a search at
16 MiB per file, 256 MiB in total or 1,000 matches; the picker says when a
limit was reached.
